5,"title":"1.2","description":"","creator":{"login":"knolleary","id":51083,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51083?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/knolleary","html_url":"https://github.com/knolleary","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knolleary/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knolleary/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knolleary/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knolleary/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knolleary/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knolleary/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knolleary/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knolleary/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knolleary/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":29,"state":"closed","created_at":"2020-06-29T21:54:23Z","updated_at":"2026-06-10T14:09:05Z","due_on":"2020-09-30T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2021-08-27T10:56:50Z"},"comments":7,"created_at":"2020-03-23T12:45:29Z","updated_at":"2026-06-10T14:06:57Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":{"id":425387,"node_id":"IT_kwDOAFIGrc4ABn2r","name":"Feature","description":"A request, idea, or new functionality","color":"blue","created_at":"2024-01-25T09:46:49Z","updated_at":"2024-10-08T08:43:27Z","is_enabled":true},"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!--\r\nThis issue tracker is for problems with the Node-RED runtime, the editor or the core nodes.\r\n\r\nIf your issue is:\r\n  - a general 'how-to' type question,\r\n  - a feature request or suggestion for a change,\r\n  - or problems with 3rd party (`node-red-contrib-`) nodes\r\n\r\nplease use the [Node-RED Forum](https://discourse.nodered.org) or [slack team](https://nodered.org/slack).\r\n\r\nYou could also consider asking a question on [Stack Overflow](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/node-red) and tag it `node-red`.\r\n\r\nThat way the whole Node-RED user community can help, rather than rely on the core development team.\r\n\r\nTo help us understand the issue, please fill-in as much of the following information as you can:\r\n-->\r\n\r\n### What are the steps to reproduce?\r\n\r\nCreate two git branches for one Node-RED project and try to merge one **big** file flows.json from that different branches. Please note that this is not reproducing if flows.json file is small.\r\n\r\n### What happens?\r\n\r\nGit does not try to merge files into one, just replacing one file with another.\r\n\r\nI even know why that happens. It is because Node-RED save flows.json to git as one string without any formatting: EOL and any other delimiters. Just adding one EOF. I understand, that It is right for Node-RED to save JSON in compact view. But this creates a problem to git compatibility. Could you please provide an option (maybe  managed through settings.js, for example) to save flows.json in formatted view for git?\r\n\r\n### What do you expect to happen?\r\n\r\ngit should see changed lines (like the \"diff\" tool) from different branches.\r\n\r\n### Please tell us about your environment:\r\n\r\n- [  ] Node-RED version: 1.0.2\r\nReproduce in any other environment.\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/node-red/node-red/issues/2515/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/node-red/node-red/issues/2515/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}